CS:FlmToolEquipment^WEB^Global Data^N^N
	CS:assistant.AddTaskCardsToWorkOrderAssistant^WEB^Global Data^N^N
		CS:$this^WEB^Wizard Step^N^N
			A:$this^Add Task Cards To Work Order^
		CE:
		CS:assistantsteps.assistantcancelledstep^WEB^Wizard Step^N^N
			A:assistantcancelledstep^Cancelled^
		CE:
		CS:assistantsteps.assistantfinalstep^WEB^Wizard Step^N^N
			A:assistantfinalstep^Finished^
		CE:
		CS:assistantsteps.assistantstep.-1391464638^WEB^Wizard Step^N^N
			A:assistantstep^Predefined Task Cards^
		CE:
		CS:assistantsteps.assistantstep.1590128308^WEB^Wizard Step^N^N
			A:assistantstep^Manual Tasks^
		CE:
		CS:assistantsteps.assistantstep.assistantcontent.markdowntext.textproperty.1017935693^WEB^Message^N^N
			A:textproperty^In this step, you can manually enter a task(s) to work order.^
		CE:
		CS:assistantsteps.assistantstep.assistantcontent.markdowntext.textproperty.1469729481^WEB^Message^N^N
			A:textproperty^If the Use Execution Logic option is turned on, the predefined task card will be included on a work order based on existing grouping criteria.\005Cn            This means that the added task cards and subtasks can be created on different work orders that the one you are working on. ^
		CE:
		CS:assistantsteps.assistantstep.assistantcontent.markdowntext.textproperty.1911803888^WEB^Message^N^N
			A:textproperty^If the Use Execution Logic option is turned on, the manually entered task(s) will be added to the Ungrouped Task Cards ELO as well as the corresponding work order. ^
		CE:
		CS:assistantsteps.assistantstep.assistantcontent.markdowntext.textproperty.374933911^WEB^Message^N^N
			A:textproperty^In this step, select the predefined task card(s) that is to be included on the work order generated from Fleet and Asset Management.\005Cn            All active task cards that are valid for the selected serial will be listed here. When a task card is included, all belonging information such as\005Cn            resources, material and subtasks will be transferred to the work order.^
		CE:
	CE:
